# GitHub does not know what a .klv file is, and cannot be made to until the
# language sees real use -- Linguist only accepts new languages with evidence
# of adoption across many repositories. Until then, this override borrows an
# existing grammar so policy files render with some colour instead of as a
# grey block, which is what an unrecognised extension looks like.
#
# The cost: GitHub counts .klv files as INI in the repository language stats.
# Acceptable for now. Remove this line the day Kelvra is in Linguist.
#
# Locally, editors/vscode/ ships a real TextMate grammar for .klv.
*.klv linguist-language=INI

# Documentation, not code -- keep it out of the language stats.
*.md linguist-documentation

# Normalise line endings. The repo is developed on Windows and tested on
# Linux CI; without this the two disagree on every file.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
